## unreleased ##
    - Helper.parent and child: ~init and ~malloc create the outputs, for C
      values initialized in memory given by the caller (FLINT contexts and
      their elements); ~parent_last; the init of a child gets the C variable
      of its parent (with_parent ~c)

## 0.3 ##
  Highlights:
    - the order of the steps of a stub is computed by Plan.schedule, written
      and proved in Why3 (proof/) against a specification of the memory as
      blocks: no leak, no double free, no use after free, GC roots, noalloc,
      runtime lock. Each generated stub is also checked at generation time
      with an OCaml model of the memory (Blocks). A work in progress: the
      specification is high-level (proof/memory.mlw, a lower-level model, is
      not used yet) and the printing of the C code is not proved
    - memory safety fixes: fixed_length_array/string read out of bounds
      on a short input; a raising conversion leaked the inputs already
      copied (conversions no longer raise, checks run first); leaks in
      algdata fields and array elements
    - new helpers: value_type (C++-like classes), enum, flags, nullable,
      keep_alive/parent/child, exception_, extra_input, and Helper.func
      ~error, ~release_lock, ~noalloc
    - the minimum OCaml version is 4.14

  Breaking changes:
    - module Type renamed Ty; the constructor and destructor arguments are
      init and clear everywhere (Expert.mk_init, Expert.mk_clear)
    - int_trunc, input/output_string, input/output_array renamed c_int,
      string_len(_ref), array_len(_ref) (old names deprecated)
    - string_nt fails on a null byte (old behaviour: string_nt_prefix)
    - the get, set and internal options of Helper.abstract, custom and
      custom_ptr are removed (still in Expert)

  Other changes:
    - Ty.mlc.contract describes a type for the scheduler (owned_by_ml,
      ml_heap, effects of ml2c and c2ml)
    - ?dispose (OCaml function run before collection) and ?mem
      (caml_alloc_custom_mem) for custom types and value_type
    - algdata: pattern matching macros in the style of datatype99, the
      fields given to t_mk_C are moved
    - an input holding unregistered OCaml values is converted last
    - static custom_operations, and identical C definitions printed once:
      several stub files can be linked together
    - Expert.abstract takes expressions for icty and cty
    - fixes that didn't compile or were wrong: string_len free, convert,
      ignored_result, bigarray_array1 to C
    - the examples of the documentation are compiled and run (tests/doc);
      documentation of the memory model

## 0.2 Second initial release ##
    - implement algdata as input
    - fix tests in release mode for ocaml < 5.2

## 0.1 Initial release ##

